{title: Jesus, Tender Shepherd, Hear Me}
{artist: Mary L. Duncan / John Stainer}
{genre: Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: jesus-tender-shepherd-hear-me.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Jesus_Tender_Shepherd_Hear_Me-Evening_Prayer)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus, [Am]ten[C7]der [F]Shepherd, hear me;
[F]Bless Thy little [C]lamb [F]to[C]night;
[F]Through the [C7]darkness [F]be [Dm]Thou [A7]near me;
[Dm]Watch my [F]sleep [C7]till morning [F]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]All this [Am]day [C7]Thy [F]hand has led me,
[F]And I thank Thee [C]for [F]Thy [C]care;
[F]Thou hast [C7]clothed me, [F]warmed [Dm]and [A7]fed me,
[Dm]Listen [F]to [C7]my evening [F]prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Let my [Am]sins [C7]be [F]all forgiven;
[F]Bless the friends I [C]love [F]so [C]well;
[F]Take me, [C7]when I [F]die, [Dm]to [A7]Heaven,
[Dm]Happy [F]there [C7]with Thee to [F]dwell.
{end_of_verse}
